Gene genomic coordinates for CNV inference (sc_infercnv, run.ml_SCEVAN).

Files
    gene_chr_hg19.txt   30238 human genes, GRCh37
    gene_chr_hg38.txt   29902 human genes, GRCh38
    gene_chr_mm10.txt   28852 mouse genes, GRCm38

Format: tab separated, no header, four columns

    EnsemblID    Chromosome    Start    Stop

Rows are pre-sorted by chromosome (1..22 human, 1..19 mouse) and then by
start position, which is the order the CNV moving average expects. Only
autosomes are included; sex chromosomes and scaffolds were dropped
upstream because their copy number is confounded by donor sex.

Source: scCancer2 (MIT), inst/txt/gene-chr-*.txt
    https://github.com/czythu/scCancer
    Guo et al., Brief Bioinform 2021;22(3):bbaa127
    Chen et al., Bioinformatics 2024;40(2):btae028

Ensembl IDs are mapped to gene symbols at load time by
pkg.e_genecoordinates, using assets/Ensembl/Ensembl_<species>_genes.mat.
